tical radius has length $b=8.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{8}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-115126" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4002192580b9b7fe1d7bfc3cd2faaf10bb17a991358e13635deb7b3050f65a2b"} {"question" "q-115126" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-115126" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-115126" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}=1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-277923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the ellipse \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{81}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-277923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=64$ and ${b}^{2}=81.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=64,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{64}=8.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=81,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{81}=9.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=9,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=8.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 8=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-277923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4002192580b9b7fe1d7bfc3cd2faaf10bb17a991358e13635deb7b3050f65a2b"} {"question" "q-277923" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-277923" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-277923" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-277923" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-279197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-279197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=12$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=12,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-279197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4002192580b9b7fe1d7bfc3cd2faaf10bb17a991358e13635deb7b3050f65a2b"} {"question" "q-279197" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-279197" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070132/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b9e709e1228d2028408cd0af2ea933dff2d1094ada4785db8c35647a6c7d958"} {"question" "q-279197" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer